 {:href "/athletes/121929"} "Ma Long"] " became the most decorated table tennis player in Olympic history. The two other member of the Chinese team were " [:a {:href "/athletes/1800098"} "Fan Zhendong"] ", gold medalist in the men’s singles, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2502769"} "Wang Chuqin"] ", gold medalist in the mixed doubles. The surprise silver medalist was No.7 seed Sweden, led by " [:a {:href "/athletes/2504051"} "Truls Möregårdh"] ", silver medalist from the individual competition. France, led by the Lebrun brothers, secured the bronze medal, defeating a valiant Japan 3-2. This was France’s first-ever medal in the team event at the Olympics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "People's Republic of China"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/1800098"} "Fan Zhendong"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/121929"} "Ma Long"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/2502769"} "Wang Chuqin"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Sweden"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/146777"} "Anton Källberg"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136031"} "Kristian Karlsson"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/2504051"} "Truls Möregårdh"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} "France"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertica